{"taxClaims":[{"text":"The cost and running expenses of a motor car are disallowed expenses under Regulation 27 of the GST (General) Regulations. Hence, the GST incurred on the purchase and running expenses (e.g. petrol and parking expenses) of a motor car is not claimable, except where the car is excluded from the definition of a 'motor car' in Regulation 25(1) of the GST (General) Regulations.","recordId":"LIVE_TOPIC_iras-gst-motor-vehicles_e0039b80a205","quote":"The cost and running expenses of a motor car are disallowed expenses under Regulation 27 of the GST (General) Regulations. Hence, the GST incurred on the purchase and running expenses (e.g. petrol and parking expenses) of a motor car is not claimable, except where the car is excluded from the definition of a 'motor car' in Regulation 25(1) of the GST (General) Regulations.","kind":"RULE"}],
 "treatment":"Property, plant and equipment acquisition of a passenger car",
 "requiredAccounts":[{"accountName":"Motor Vehicles","category":"ASSET","debitCredit":"DEBIT","rationale":"To record the acquisition cost of the motor vehicle including any non-recoverable GST."}]}

